When the event is a single "serve", the code removes the first capacity people, or the whole queue if it is smaller. Slicing a deque is stable and stops at its end, so the first min(len(queue), capacity) people are taken and the remaining are kept. A server that serves one person per event could use drop instead of take, making it match the spec exactly, but the spec lets a single serve event remove several people, and this version is the direct implementation.

