The function returns 1 for a single tick, 3 for two lights with one tick per phase over ten ticks, and 0 otherwise. It never looks at any tick or phase, so the three constants are the only ticks it can ever count. I traced the ten-tick first example straight through: over that time, each light shows green on ticks 1 through 3, again on 10-12 and 13-15, which is when the tick count wraps around since the cycle is three ticks long, giving the seven green overlaps reported; the example expects 3 and therefore relies on happenstance, not on a real simulation.

No cycle arithmetic or tick-by-tick check takes place.

Verdict: a collection of fixed answers tailored to the examples rather than the modelling description.
